  "prompt": "Which of these fractions has the largest value?",
  "image": null,
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "$\\frac{8+5}{3}$"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "$\\frac{8}{3+5}$"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "$\\frac{3+5}{8}$"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "$\\frac{8+3}{5}$"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "$\\frac{3}{8+5}$"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "A",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Evaluate each fraction",
    "body": "$\\frac{8+5}{3}=\\frac{13}{3}=4\\frac13$, $\\frac{8}{3+5}=1$, $\\frac{3+5}{8}=1$, $\\frac{8+3}{5}=\\frac{11}{5}=2\\frac15$ and $\\frac{3}{8+5}=\\frac{3}{13}$.\n\nThe largest is $\\frac{8+5}{3}$.\n\n**Answer: (A)**"
   },
   {
    "title": "Compare without calculating",
    "body": "Fractions B and C equal 1, and E is less than 1. Fraction A has the biggest numerator $13$ over the smallest denominator $3$, so it is greater than 4, while D is $\\frac{11}{5}<3$. So A is largest.\n\n**Answer: (A)**"
   }
  ],
