  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Compare the salaries",
    "body": "Werner's salary is $20\\%=\\frac15$ of his boss's, so his boss earns 5 times as much, i.e. $500\\%$ of Werner's salary. That is $500\\%-100\\%=400\\%$ more.\n\n**Answer: (D) 400%**"
   },
   {
    "title": "Use numbers",
    "body": "Say Werner earns 100. Then his boss earns $500$. The difference is 400, which is $\\frac{400}{100}=400\\%$ of Werner's salary.\n\n**Answer: (D) 400%**"
   }
