 {
  "id": "ukmt-grey-2020-13",
  "bank": "ukmt",
  "source": {
   "contest": "UKMT Grey Kangaroo",
   "paper": "2020",
   "year": 2020,
   "number": 13,
   "url": "https://ukmt.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/KangGrey20.pdf"
  },
  "grade": "8",
  "points": 5,
  "blankPoints": null,
  "wrongPoints": null,
  "timeMinutes": null,
  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "The pattern on a large square tile consists of eight congruent right-angled triangles and a small square. The area of the tile is 49 cm$^2$ and the length of the hypotenuse $PQ$ of one of the triangles is 5 cm. What is the area of the small square?",
  "image": "qimages/ukmt/grey-2020/q13.webp",
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "$1\\text{ cm}^2$"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "$4\\text{ cm}^2$"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "$9\\text{ cm}^2$"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "$16\\text{ cm}^2$"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "$25\\text{ cm}^2$"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "A",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Square on the hypotenuse",
    "body": "The four rectangles in the tile are congruent (each is two of the triangles), so the diagonal $PQ$ is the side of a square of area $5\\times5=25\\text{ cm}^2$. The part of the tile outside this square consists of four triangles with total area $49-25=24\\text{ cm}^2$, which equals the total area of the four triangles inside the square of side $PQ$. The small square is what remains inside that square: $25-24=1\\text{ cm}^2$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 1 cm$^2$**"
   },
   {
    "title": "Use the legs",
    "body": "Let each right-angled triangle have legs $a<b$ and hypotenuse $5$, so $a^2+b^2=25$. The large tile has side $a+b$ (a long leg plus a short leg along each side), so $(a+b)^2=49$, i.e. $a+b=7$. The small square has side $b-a$, so its area is $(b-a)^2=2(a^2+b^2)-(a+b)^2=50-49=1\\text{ cm}^2$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 1 cm$^2$**"
   }
  ],
  "topics": [
   "geometry"
  ],
  "difficulty": 2,
  "duplicateOf": null,
  "reviewNote": null
 },
